{# Body of the managed block written into /etc/default/sentinel. No header comment
   and no trailing marker: blockinfile supplies both, and this file is a block
   inside a package-owned file rather than a file of its own.

   It lives in a template rather than inline in the task so that the rendering
   can be checked without a host — see tests/render/. The two defects this
   escaping exists to prevent were both invisible to lint and found by reading
   rendered output.

   Values are single-quoted, because this file has two consumers with one shared
   hazard: systemd parses it, and upstream's container.init sources it as shell.
   An unquoted value carrying a space, a double quote, a `$` or a `#` mangles the
   environment for the first and can be executed by the second.
   PYROSCOPE_HTTP_HEADERS, which takes JSON for multi-tenant setups, is the
   everyday case. Neither consumer expands anything inside single quotes, so JSON,
   spaces and `$` all pass through with no escaping to get wrong. The one value
   they cannot carry is a single quote, which the task asserts against. #}
EXTRA_JAVA_OPTS='-javaagent:{{ opennms_sentinel_pyroscope_jar }}'
{% for key, value in opennms_sentinel_pyroscope.items() %}
{{ key }}='{{ value }}'
{% endfor %}
